# LeakSanitizer suppressions for known-benign, out-of-our-hands leak classes. Keep this list
# SHORT and each entry justified -- a suppression that could hide a real Mosaic leak is worse
# than a red suite.

# putenv() hands ownership of the string to the process environment for the program's lifetime;
# FLTK's Fl_Posix_System_Driver::putenv strdups internally (test_theme.cpp exercises the FLTK
# scheme override). LSan flags the strings at exit by design. Not fixable from the caller side.
leak:Fl_Posix_System_Driver::putenv

# fontconfig keeps global caches that are only released by FcFini(), which FLTK (by upstream
# decision) never calls. One-time, bounded, process-lifetime allocations.
leak:libfontconfig
